.page true 1 do nothing, successfully
.alias :

# SYNOPSIS
*true*
*:*

# DESCRIPTION
`true` ignores its arguments and exits with status 0. gapsh also has `true` and `:` as builtins that do the same; `:` is handy as an empty command in loops (`while :; do ...; done`).

# EXAMPLES
    while true; do date; sleep 1; done
    if true; then echo yes; fi

# SEE ALSO
false(1), gapsh(1)
